On the same lines as Dan's posting on realistic dog behavior, a friend
and I (this was such a brainstorm!  Too cool idea, the game will never
be the same), were thinking that the dog should bark when hungry.
This would have the same effect as stepping on a squeaky board.  He
could also bark to wake you up when resting (with a repeat count), and
a monster enters the room.  Maybe even wake you when sleeping from a trap.

We need to make our pets more worth while.  Too often these pets are
mistreated by thier owners.  Perhaps the People for the Ethical
Treatment of Animals radicals should appear and either attack or throw
eggs (or simply blow up a nearby laboratory).  

Along these lines, as we all know, dogs and cats mate and have
puppies and kittens.  These offspring would become your pets as well.

This is my friends idea, so don't flame me.  I had nothing to do with
this.  Dog and cat doo-doo could be extremely useful.  Having a pet,
you could collect lots of it.  You eat it and thereby vomit.  Write 
the E word with it (lasts alot longer).  Apply it, and have the same
effect as scare monster.  Throw it, and cause blindness.  Defile
alters with it.  By dipping it in potions, create potions of sickness.
Placing doo-doo on top of a pile of loot would protect it from being
stolen by humanoid creatures.  Dipping your weapon (or hand) into it,
would have the same effect as reading a scroll of confuse monster (the
monsters are overcome by the fumes).  It might have a few harmful
effects, such as offering it would have detrimental effects, and while
carrying it, your charisma is lowered, and you lose stealth.
